      "title": "Why the definition matters",
      "narration": "Rosa, an electrician, injures her shoulder and can no longer climb or pull wire. She could manage a hardware store or estimate jobs from a desk. Is she disabled? The answer depends entirely on how her policy defines the word. Disability income insurance does not pay because a person is hurt; it pays because the person meets the policy’s definition of total or partial disability. Two policies with identical benefit amounts can produce opposite claim decisions on the same injury. Before quoting any disability policy, a producer reads the definition and explains it in the client’s own terms.",
